{
 "fps": 30,
 "frames": 1350,
 "dur": 45.0,
 "target": 45.0,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Why was Lady Liberty's arm standing alone in a New York park?",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 3.316
  },
  {
   "text": "People paid to climb inside it, all the way up to the torch.",
   "s": 3.616,
   "e": 6.465
  },
  {
   "text": "And if nobody paid, the rest of her might never cross the ocean.",
   "s": 6.665,
   "e": 9.661
  },
  {
   "text": "Because her head was sitting in Paris, and her body didn't exist yet.",
   "s": 9.861,
   "e": 12.918
  },
  {
   "text": "New Yorkers laughed. One newspaper joked: a piece of a statue beats no statue.",
   "s": 13.118,
   "e": 17.438
  },
  {
   "text": "Then it got worse: for six years, the arm stood there, alone.",
   "s": 17.638,
   "e": 20.511
  },
  {
   "text": "Kids picnicked under it. Pigeons nested in the torch.",
   "s": 20.711,
   "e": 23.334
  },
  {
   "text": "So why build the arm first? It was an advertisement.",
   "s": 23.734,
   "e": 26.279
  },
  {
   "text": "Every ticket paid for one more piece of her.",
   "s": 26.479,
   "e": 28.437
  },
  {
   "text": "France built the statue for free, but America had to pay for her pedestal.",
   "s": 28.637,
   "e": 32.354
  },
  {
   "text": "And nobody wanted to. Until one newspaper begged every reader for a dollar.",
   "s": 32.554,
   "e": 36.597
  },
  {
   "text": "Kids sent pennies. Over a hundred thousand people chipped in.",
   "s": 36.797,
   "e": 39.323
  },
  {
   "text": "Ten years after the arm, the rest of Lady Liberty finally showed up.",
   "s": 39.523,
   "e": 43.27
  }
 ],
